Include base/logging.h in the file that calls LOG(ERROR).

The presandbox hook has exactly one LOG() call -- the radeonsi dlopen
failure path -- and has never included the header that declares it. It
builds anyway everywhere upstream compiles it, because every such
configuration is ash-chrome, where base/logging.h arrives transitively
through the VA-API includes guarded by BUILDFLAG(USE_VAAPI).

This fork is the configuration upstream's own TODO at the top of the
file describes and does not test: hardware video decoding with V4L2 and
without VA-API. USE_VAAPI is off, that include block is skipped, and
the transitive path to base/logging.h disappears with it:

  error: use of undeclared identifier 'ERROR'

So add the include the file's own code requires, rather than making it
depend on a buildflag that has nothing to do with logging. Ordered
alphabetically among the base/ includes, which is where IWYU and the
style guide both put it.

--- a/media/gpu/sandbox/hardware_video_decoding_sandbox_hook_linux.cc
+++ b/media/gpu/sandbox/hardware_video_decoding_sandbox_hook_linux.cc
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 #include <dlfcn.h>
 #include <sys/stat.h>
 
+#include "base/logging.h"
 #include "base/process/process_metrics.h"
 #include "base/strings/stringprintf.h"
 #include "build/build_config.h"
